  "step_3": "The decision reason relies on counting how many outcomes exceed the unweighted average of all distinct outcomes (1633.33), favoring the lottery with more such outcomes—in this case, Lottery B. However, the individual does not mention or imply any such calculation. They do not refer to an average of outcomes, nor do they count how many outcomes exceed a threshold. Instead, they contrast expected value reasoning with a preference for certainty and express discomfort with the 1% chance of zero in B. Their justification centers on risk aversion and the emotional or decisional weight of guaranteed outcomes, not on the number of outcomes above a computed mean. There is no overlap in the information used (e.g., no mention of average outcome or counts) or in the decision rule (risk avoidance vs. counting high outcomes). Therefore, the decision reason is not reflected in the verbal report.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
}

